{
  "body": "`store` in `src/tide_cache.py` keeps every tide reading for ever. Readings should expire after a retention period, but how long the harbour keeps a reading is a policy call the repository does not state. Expire stale readings once the period is known.\n\n**Delivers:** Readings held past the retention period no longer stay in `READINGS` (`src/tide_cache.py:1`): `store` (`src/tide_cache.py:4`), today an unconditional append (`src/tide_cache.py:5`), also drops every reading older than that period. The period itself is the open question below. A reading has no timestamp of its own (`src/tide_cache.py:4`), so age is measured from when `store` received it.\n\n**Test contract:** Failing tests first. A reading younger than the retention period survives a later `store`. A reading older than the period is gone after a later `store`. The boundary (a reading exactly at the period) follows the decided wording. Newly stored readings are always kept. The clock is injected or faked, so no test sleeps.\n\n**Files:** `src/tide_cache.py` (modified); a new test file, since the repository has no test surface yet.\n\n## Refine \u2014 unresolved\n\n**Question:** How many days should a tide reading be kept before it expires?\n\n**Evidence gathered:** `src/tide_cache.py:4` and `src/tide_cache.py:5` store every reading with no expiry, and `src/tide_cache.py:1` is the only storage. `README.md:3` states no policy, and neither do the other files under `src/`. A wide vault search found no area profile, ADR, decision or lesson on retention; the fixture specs `[[spec/fixture-upfront-answer-spec]]` and `[[spec/fixture-tide-expiry-spec]]` hold no content on it. A sibling record, `[[task/tide-cache-expire-stale-readings-leftover-answer]]`, carries an operator answer of its own; it belongs to that record, so it is not adopted here.\n\n**Recommended answer:** 30 days, kept from the earlier draft as a common retention for operational readings. This is a default only: nothing in the repository or vault supports it, and the harbour's own policy should override it.\n**Answer:** Make it 60 days.\n",
